    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d652">

                <pb facs="0941" n="813" xml:id="pg813"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">820.7961 Dept. of Commerce Flight/16:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grant-Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-02-02T12:00:00-03:30"><hi rendition="#italic">February 2,
                                1928—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received February 2—11:10
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>7. Your telegram No. 1 of January 7, 8 p.m.<anchor n="91" xml:id="d652-f1"/> The
                    Uruguayan Government has granted permission flight to visit Uruguay and to pass
                    over its territories.</p>
                <p>It is suggested that the use of the word “pathfinding” might give rise to
                    misunderstanding.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grant-Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
